**You can get the kill counter up by using a Tarantula grinder, in which you place down [[Tarantula Minion]]s as they have a much shorter action time than [[Spider Minion]]s and slay the tarantulas they spawn to increase the number of kills on the armor.
Note: This tip can be moved to Tarantula Armor page.-->
**Alternatively, a high damaging set such as {{Item|Superior Dragon Armor}} or {{Item|Shadow Assassin Armor}} sets is a sizable improvement over {{Item|Tarantula Armor}} in {{stat|dmg}}, and it can decrease the time for each slayer by a measurable amount, due to it focusing on {{stat|dmg}} rather than {{stat|def}}.
*A {{Item|Radiant Power Orb}} or higher, paired with a {{Item|Spider Hat}} is recommended for fighting '''Tarantula Broodfather''' {{SlayerTier|III}} and above, as an alternative to {{Item|Tarantula Armor}}.
*It is highly recommended to use Healing [[Enchantments]] like {{Ench|Life Steal}} and {{Ench|Vampirism}} on weapons. If the [[player]]'s {{stat|hp}} gets too low while fighting a '''Tarantula Broodfather''', killing a couple of nearby spiders can activate {{Ench|Vampirism}} and keep the [[player]] alive.<!--
* If killing the [[Mutant Tarantula]] is too difficult to kill using melee due to its ludicrous damage and high health, you can knock it to an edge with a [[Runaan's Bow]] or another bow with a high projectile rate and knock it off, making it take fall damage, making it much easier to finish off.
**The [[Mutant Tarantula]] has a health amount of 576k, however it can take a large percentage of its health-bar after falling from a decent height, because the enemy mob's fall damage scales to its health.
Note: These 2 tips should be moved to Mutant Tarantula page.-->
*While fighting the '''Tarantula Broodfather''', backing up into a corner reduces the effect of its leaps and makes it much easier to land hits on the boss. 
*If the [[player]] has a high amount of {{stat|int}}, a {{Item|Voodoo Doll}} can be used to drain the '''Tarantula Broodfather'''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s {{stat|hp}} quickly.<!--
*Using an [[Aspect of the End]], [[Grappling Hook]], or [[Tarantula Boots]] will make traversal of the [[Spider's Den|Spider's]] den significantly easier.
**These items are extremely useful, as the [[Spider's Den]] is made up of many layers with chains of [[Web|Cobwebs]] running through them, which these items can help avoid and are useful for scaling the vertical mountain.-->
*It used to be possible to sword-swap between a {{Item|Giant's Sword}} and a {{Item|Scorpion Foil}} to one-shot a '''Tarantula Broodfather''' {{Stier|4}}. This method is no longer available, however, as since sword-swapping has since been patched.
*While the bats themselves are immune to Magic Damage, the ability from {{Item|Giant's Sword}} counts as melee and it can be used to clear them.
*Since the release of 0.23.5, it is recommended to bring a {{Item|Spider Shortbow}} or better to deal with Egg Sacs at higher tiers.
**On a {{Gamemode|Ironman}} profile, is recommended to grind {{Stier|3}} bosses until one obtains {{Item|Spider Catalyst|amount=3}} to craft one, as it is much rarer from higher tiers.
*When dealing with the '''Tarantula Broodfather''' {{Stier|5}}, it is recommended to be aware of multiple {{MobSprite|Arachne's Keeper}}s as the combination of their Venom Shot and the Broodfather's Noxious Paralysis will quickly drain the player's current health.
*Using a [[Tarantula Pet]] and/or [[Tarantula Armor|Tarantula]]/[[Primordial Armor|Primordial]] Chestplate is very useful for combating Noxious Paralysis.
*The best area to spawn the '''Tarantula Broodfather''' quickly is the [[Burning Desert]] in the [[Crimson Isle]] by killing [[Flaming Spider|Flaming Spiders]] .

